  It's two-handed.  That means it's a deathtrap if it gets cursed in
Gehennom.  (No, you cannot cast the spell of Remove Curse when you're
wielding a cursed two-handed weapon.  No, you cannot loot or apply any
container when wielding a cursed two-handed weapon.  No, you cannot
successfully #pray in Gehennom.)

  Being two-handed also costs you 6-9 points of AC due to lack of
shield.  (Easy to enchant elven shields to +7.  Small shields for spell
casters litter the ground after you finish Fort Ludios and/or the
Castle.)

  It's also no better than an ordinary quarterstaff against demons,
ghosts, shades, all LMVWZ, were-creatures and Death.   That's 3.5 base
dmg, +2 Expert damage, +7 enchantment, +3 Str dmg = 15.5 dmg.  That's
not great, especially for a two-handed weapon.  (Under the same
circumstances thrown poisoned darts will average 36 dmg, with a 10%
chance of instakill.)

  OTOH, hungerless regen is not bad to have welded to your hands.
Level-drain resistance isn't necessary with MC3.  The Staff can also be
invoked whether wielded or not.  It's the inability to access your BoH
that will really hurt.

  Rodney will try to steal it if you're a healer.   That can make it
into a worse deathtrap.  (Two-handed artifact weapons from your Quest
are nasty tricks played on your role by the DevTeam.  And I mean
*nasty*.)

  So it's a great weapon until you reach the VotD (mostly undead).  Then
it gets worse and worse up until the point that Rodney steals it.


  (Hey, I want to like the weapon.  The DevTeam are the ones who turned
it into a deathtrap.)

  Magicbane, Grimtooth, a silver dagger (wishable), even a crysknife
look like better wielded weapons.  Can still carry the Staff for
